/ json-lines: plang's json is written formatted by default, so what writes one record per line writes JSON Lines.
/ This goal is the plan's index and its proof: each stage is a goal, each comment a behaviour we want, and the step
/ under it runs the test that proves it. Each test goes red before its stage. The text is start.md.
Start
- call Stage1
- call Stage2
- call Stage3

Stage1
/ a .jsonl file reads as the list of its lines, each a json value — plang test /plan/json-lines/app/type/jsonl/ReadsItsLines
- call /plan/json-lines/app/type/jsonl/ReadsItsLines
/ a list saved to .jsonl and read back is the same list, one element per line — plang test RoundTrip
- call /plan/json-lines/app/type/jsonl/RoundTrip
/ a dict is one record, never its entries; a text holding a newline stays one line — C# test JsonlKindTests
/ (ADict_IsOneRecord, ANewlineInAValue_StaysOneLine)
/ CR LF lines read, a blank line is skipped, a line that is no json is refused naming its number — C# test
/ JsonlKindTests (CrLfLines_Read, ABlankLine_IsSkipped, ABadLine_IsRefused_NamingItsNumber)

Stage2
/ errors.jsonl keeps one record per line with json formatted — C# test WindowErrorsTests (ARecord_IsOneLine)
/ the cursor line is one line beside the frames, ended once — C# test HeadlessCursorTests (TheCursor_IsOneLine_EndedOnce)

Stage3
/ json is written formatted by default, compact when the setting says — plang test
/ /plan/json-lines/app/type/json/FormatSetting
- call /plan/json-lines/app/type/json/FormatSetting
/ the setting never reaches plang's wire, a digest or a .pr — C# test JsonFormatSettingTests
/ (TheWire_IsUntouched, ADigest_IsUntouched, APr_IsUntouched)
/ a saved llm answer is served whichever way its file was written — C# test LlmAnswersFileTests
/ (ACompactFile_IsServed_WhenFormatted, AFormattedFile_IsServed_WhenCompact)
